The butler is moving to the dining patio.

Chameleon: Aw, is that really all you can say? I'd love to hear more details on
your experiments, like exposing human subjects to radio-polonium-infused
animals.

Malatesta: Oh, the human subjects! Yes, I'd love to talk about the human
subjects, that would be just lovely. Anything you want to know. I'm afraid we
had to end those experiments.

Chameleon: End them? How come?

Malatesta: The results were just too unpredictable. So much variation between
subjects, even when infected from exactly the same specimen. Every one of them
showed some kind of effect, but the details of those effects were so scattered,
we couldn't get a p-value low enough to publish.

